# =============================================================================
# compile_commands.json generation (per ADR-0018 style guide)
# =============================================================================
# TIANSHU uses kiron1/bazel-compile-commands (Bazel official recommendation).
# It's a standalone binary, NOT a Bazel dep, so users install it separately:
#
#   Install (one of):
#     go install github.com/kiron1/bazel-compile-commands/cmd/bazel-compile-commands@latest
#     # or download from https://github.com/kiron1/bazel-compile-commands/releases
#     # or build from source: bazel build --config=gnu //bcc:bazel-compile-commands
#
#   Generate (run from repo root):
#     bazel-compile-commands
#
# Why not hedron/helly25 fork:
#   - hedron upstream inactive since 2024-06 (team joined Google DeepMind)
#   - helly25 fork: "restricted maintenance" since 2026-05, uses Python
#   - kiron1: C++ (no Python dep), Bazel 9 fully compatible, MIT, maintained
#
# Refs:
#   - https://bazel.build/install/ide
#   - https://github.com/kiron1/bazel-compile-commands
